# Attendance Help — locked working state

## Restore if camera/UI work breaks WebRTC
- Branch: `checkpoint/webrtc-screen-ok`
- Tag: `checkpoint-webrtc-screen-ok`
- Doc: `docs/CHECKPOINT_WEBRTC_SCREEN.md`

## Confirmed working (do not break)
- REMOTE offers, CONTROL answers (initial PeerConnection)
- Screen share: MediaProjection → VideoTrack → CONTROL SurfaceViewRenderer
- DataChannel `"control"` created by REMOTE; CONTROL receives via onDataChannel
- Session connected only when PeerConnection CONNECTED + DataChannel OPEN (+ CONTROL has video)

## Camera product rules (next feature)
1. Both cameras start/stop together when camera session is active
2. CONTROL UI shows CONTROL's own local camera preview
3. REMOTE UI shows CONTROL's camera stream (same face)
4. REMOTE camera stays ON while session active (not shown on CONTROL in v1)
5. Camera renegotiation may use CONTROL createOffer only for adding camera track — do not change initial screen-share offerer role

## UI
- Do not show WebRTC debug diagnostics panel in normal UI
- STUN 701 timeouts are non-fatal when transport already CONNECTED
